The Ray Linux host draws its own window controls in every window it hosts. Its Settings and Import windows are
legacy app windows (TYPE_APP with an app name and no web app controller), so on X11 Chromium asked the window manager
for its frame and the window showed both the manager's title bar and Ray's controls, and with a custom frame it
drew a title bar of its own, its window icon (the product logo) over the window's top-left corner, and the 3 dip
extra top border Linux adds to windows without a tab strip as a band of frame colour above the page. The host names
such windows through g_ray_linux_frameless_app; they get Chromium's custom frame with no window title bar, no window
icon and no extra top border, so the page meets the frame's edge on all four sides. The window manager's icon for the
window is unchanged. The hook is null outside the Linux host.
